From: ReForge <noreply@reforge>
Date: Sun, 8 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fbdev: make /dev/disp (Allwinner display engine) optional

The fbdev driver opens DISPDEV_PATH (/dev/disp, the Allwinner display engine)
to drive the AD5M panel's HW backlight/brightness, and bailed out of
fbdev_init() with an early `return` when that open failed. That return happens
*before* the framebuffer is mmap'd, so LVGL never gets a buffer to paint into
and the screen stays black.

/dev/disp only exists on the real AD5M (sun8iw20 display engine). On any other
target -- notably qemu's virtio-gpu framebuffer used by the test harness, but
also any non-Allwinner panel -- it is absent, so guppyscreen rendered nothing
there even though /dev/fb0 was perfectly usable.

Make the open non-fatal: when /dev/disp is missing we lose only HW backlight /
brightness control (the DISP_LCD_* ioctls below already log-and-continue on a
bad fd), and keep rendering to /dev/fb0 as normal.

Signed-off-by: ReForge <noreply@reforge>
---
 lv_drivers/display/fbdev.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/lv_drivers/display/fbdev.c
+++ b/lv_drivers/display/fbdev.c
@@ -115,8 +115,10 @@ void fbdev_init(void)

     dispfd = open(DISPDEV_PATH, O_RDWR);
     if (dispfd == -1) {
-        perror("Error: cannot open display device");
-        return;
+        /* Non-fatal: DISPDEV_PATH (/dev/disp, the Allwinner display engine) is
+           AD5M-specific and absent under qemu virtio-gpu / any non-AD5M panel.
+           Without it we lose only HW backlight/brightness control (the ioctls
+           below already no-op on a bad fd) -- keep rendering to /dev/fb0. */
+        perror("Warning: cannot open display device (/dev/disp); backlight control disabled");
     }

 #if USE_BSD_FBDEV
